      "ambient": "Compact connected base has n>=1, rank r>=1, total dimension N=n+r>=2, and the line projectivization complement retains its infinity divisor.",
      "upper-normal-frame": "The retained Chern-normal reciprocal-norm Levi form is block diagonal at every point; the vertical radial direction is positive even when all horizontal directions fail positivity.",
      "upper-cutoff": "The retained chi(G)/G construction equals the reciprocal near zero and vanishes in an infinity-chart neighbourhood; smoothness and compact sublevels use the compact projective ambient.",
      "index-convention": "q-convexity outside a compact set in dimension N requires N-q+1 positive Levi eigenvalues; N-1 therefore requires at least two.",
      "monotonicity": "Every q<=N-1 implies N-1 convexity because its positive Levi requirement is stronger.",
      "homogeneity": "Complex-two-homogeneity includes positive real dilation G(tv)=t^2G(v).",
      "reference-comparison": "G on the compact reference unit sphere has positive minimum and finite maximum, giving global c|v|^2<=G<=C|v|^2.",
      "sphere-compactness": "The comparisons and compact base make Sigma1 compact, and real dilation gives compactness of all Sigmat.",
      "regular-level": "Euler dG(R)=2G>0 on every nonzero level, so Sigmat is a regular smooth real hypersurface.",
      "uniform-exception": "The compact exceptional K in the complement cannot accumulate on the removed zero section; reference comparisons give one epsilon for every small sphere.",
      "max-attainment": "Each continuous sphere restriction attains its finite maximum on the compact Sigma1.",
      "radial-domain": "The map (t,v)->[1:tv] is smooth on (0,epsilon) times Sigma1 and lies in the nonzero affine chart.",
      "local-Lipschitz": "On each closed interior interval times Sigma1, one bound for the radial derivative controls every sphere value and hence their maximum.",
      "proper-end": "If M(tj) were bounded with tj->0, every maximizing point would lie in one compact sublevel while accumulating on the removed section in the compact ambient; contradiction.",
      "negative-slope-interval": "Fix t1<epsilon and use M(t)->infinity to choose t0<t1 with M(t0)>M(t1).",
      "accepted-real-analysis": "A Lipschitz real function on a compact interval is absolutely continuous and equals the integral of its a.e. derivative plus its initial value; this elementary real-analysis input is explicitly used, not an external research theorem.",
      "negative-derivative": "The negative endpoint difference makes the integral derivative negative, so at least one differentiability point in the interval has negative derivative.",
      "envelope-fixed-maximizer": "At any maximizing v at that differentiability point, M(t+h)>=psi((t+h)v) with equality at zero. Division for h>0 and h<0 forces the fixed-v derivative to equal Mprime.",
      "constrained-gradient": "At a constrained maximum and regular level, dpsi vanishes on ker dG and is a real multiple lambda dG.",
      "lambda-normalization": "Along t->tv with G(v)=1, dG/dt=2t. Thus lambda=Mprime/(2t)<0; the real Euler radial vector p instead gives t Mprime/(2t^2), the same value.",
      "lagrangian-criticality": "psi-lambda G has zero full differential at p, with lambda fixed as a scalar at this point.",
      "constrained-real-Hessian": "Its restriction to Sigmat is psi minus a constant and has a maximum; zero full differential removes the acceleration term of any tangent curve, so its real Hessian is nonpositive on the tangent.",
      "complex-tangent": "A regular real hypersurface has a complex tangent hyperplane H=TSigma intersect iTSigma, of complex dimension N-1.",
      "real-to-complex": "Adding real Hessian inequalities for a tangent vector and its complex rotation gives the Levi inequality on H; the common positive normalization does not affect the sign.",
      "psh-sign": "LG>=0 and lambda<0 imply Lpsi restricted H<=lambda LG restricted H<=0.",
      "inertia": "If Lpsi has at least two positive eigenvalues, their complex positive two-plane intersects the codimension-one H nontrivially, contradicting nonpositive restriction.",
      "off-exception": "The maximizing p belongs to the chosen small Sigmat and lies outside K, where two positive eigenvalues were assumed.",
      "flat-local-frames": "Flat unitary Chern connections admit parallel holomorphic unitary frames on simply connected patches; G is the sum of fibre absolute squares in each frame.",
      "flat-global-G": "Constant unitary transitions preserve G; the descended squared norm is smooth, positive off zero, complex-two-homogeneous and psh.",
      "hopf-action": "n>=2, real 0<q<1 and complex a!=0 give the specified holomorphic bundle quotient; phase of a is allowed.",
      "hopf-descent": "b=-log|a|/logq gives q^(2b)|a|^2=1, so the squared norm descends through every deck iterate.",
      "hopf-curvature": "Normalized line curvature is -b alpha; alpha=ddc log|z|^2 has radial kernel and rank n-1 by the retained explicit Hessian.",
      "hopf-sign": "logq<0 means b has the sign of log|a|, so degree has the sign of -b.",
